Samsung has just announced its Galaxy S  10 line of smartphones and the sn+ model  is looking really impressive let's talk  about the five features that are a step  ahead of Apple's iPhone 10s for starters  the new Infinity o display is a game  changer it's very color accurate and  incredibly bright display mate measured  a peak brightness of up to 1200 nits  compared to 725 on the iPhone Tenace max  that's actually a pretty massive  difference making the S 10s display the  brightest in the industry this also  helps it achieve HDR 10 plus support  which is more widely supported than the  iPhone 10 SS Dolby vision support since  ACR 10 plus is royalty-free for video  production companies the s tens display  is also the most color accurate display  in any smartphone with slightly better  tcpip three color accuracy than Apple's  iPhone 10s Mac's we haven't yet seen the  display in person but we'll be comparing  it to the tennis Maxx as soon as we get  our hands on it from the looks of it  Apple's gonna have to add pro motion  technology to their 2019 iPhones if they  want to top Samsung's infinity o display  for the second feature it's the design  there were a few things that bugged me  about the older Samsung smartphone  designs that kept the iPhones on a step  above Samsung but all those things seem  to be finally perfected with s 10 first  of all the display is notch --less with  a hole-punch camera cutout that's cut  using a laser so the surrounding pixels  aren't damaged I've gotta admit that the  cutout looks great and it allows for a  truly edge to edge display that's  incredibly immersive the fingerprint  sensor is finally gone from the back of  the phone making it look incredibly  clean in the addition of another lens  makes the camera bump longer and more  aesthetically pleasing even better the  SN Plus gets two new ceramic finishes  that you can get if you pay for at least  512 gigabytes of storage ceramic is  harder tougher and more scratch  resistant than glass although it's  harder it can still crack like glass but  maybe not as easily the ceramic model is  also a bit heavier so it should make for  a more premium feel nonetheless I still  prefer the look of my iPhone 10s max the  design changes to the S 10 just make it  look futuristic and modern compared to  their older galaxy flagships  now let's talk about that fingerprint  sensor it's under the display so it's  completely hidden in the location is  just perfect  so convenient compared to having it on  the back the best part about it is that  it's an ultrasonic sensor instead of an  optical sensor which means that it  actually uses bursts of sound to map the  fingerprint which is similar to the  sonar waves that submarines use to map  objects underwater optical sensors  require the phone to blast light onto  your finger in order to read it the  ultrasonic sensor doesn't so you can  actually unlock the SN before you wake  the display which is honestly my  favorite part about it and it should  also be more accurate reliable and  faster than optical sensors Apple is  banking on face ID which works great but  it does have its limitations like when  it's laying flat on a table the 2019  iPhone lineup is rumored to be getting  faster face ID but we're not likely to  see an in display fingerprint sensor  until at least next year for the fourth  feature we've got the cameras inside of  the hole punch cutouts we have a 10  megapixel shooter in the s 10 capable of  shooting 4k video in a wide-angle 8  megapixel camera for depth sensing the  iPhone 10s and 10's max feature a 7  megapixel shooter limited to 1080p 60  this should ultimately make for better  selfie photos and video than with the  iPhone 10 s an exceptional depth sensing  as well on the rear the SN Plus adds a  16 megapixel ultra wide lens which makes  for some pretty awesome looking photos  with wide lens distortion correction if  you shoot 1080p video with the ultra  wide camera you get some incredible  video stabilization but it probably  crops in a good amount the best part  about the camera is that it shoots in  the same HDR 10 plus format that the  display supports which is pretty unique  since even though the iPhone 10s can  shoot great HDR video it still saves the  file in standard dynamic range we'll  have to see just how good the camera is  when we get our hands on it finally  there's a new wireless power share  feature it basically allows your s 10 to  wirelessly charge another Qi compatible  device including even their oldest  wireless charging smart phones in their  new Galaxy buds in terms of charging  your friends smartphone it doesn't seem  very practical since it renders your  phone unusable while charging and you  probably don't want your own battery to  drain down to 30% just to charge their  phone where it really makes sense is  when you want to charge your own  wearable devices like any of the galaxy  smart watches bands are most likely the  new galaxy  buds carrying case since the batteries  and those devices aren't very large you  don't risk draining your whole battery  now the most practical use case for me  is that you can actually plug the SN  into the wall and wirelessly charge  another device on top of it fast  charging 2.0 won't work through the wall  due to heat concerns but it's still  perfect for fully charging another  device and your S 10 at the same time  with only one charger you can't do this  yet with any iPhone but there are rumors  of Apple adding a similar feature to  their 2019 iPhone lineup well be getting  our hands on the Galaxy S 10 as soon as  it gets released so make sure to  subscribe so you don't miss out on those  videos
 

